  "units": "m",
  "description": "Interactive 3D scene for সরলরৈখিক গতি (linear motion, page 36, 2.2): a carrom board and a cricket ball on a lab stand. The student pushes the striker on the flat board (drags out a push arrow and lets go, or taps ধাক্কা দাও), lets the ball go (ছেড়ে দাও) or throws it sideways (ছুড়ে দাও). Each motion leaves faint pictures every 0.1 s (striker) or 0.05 s (ball, shown 4 times slower) and a dotted path, then a dashed straight line is laid through its ends: the push and the free fall lie on it (সরলরৈখিক গতি, even though the striker slows down and the ball speeds up), the sideways throw curves up to 9 cm away from it (not linear). Test tab: 5 questions (is a motion just watched linear, with the right reason; which path a pushed striker takes; what the strobe spacing means; which everyday motion is or is not linear; the definition). Phone-first, Bangla.",
  "tags": ["motion", "linear-motion", "straight-line", "free-fall", "carrom", "strobe", "bangla"],
